---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Software for community pottery studios"
	description="Kilnbook helps community and membership pottery studios share kilns, let members book wheel time, run open-studio hours and fill classes, all in one place."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">For community studios</p>
				<h1>A shared studio that runs like clockwork.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Shared kilns, members booking wheel time, open-studio hours and a class schedule on top.
					Kilnbook keeps all of it in one place, so you spend less time at the front desk and more
					time at the wheel.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/studio-floor.svg"
				alt="A community studio floor plan with wheels, hand-building tables and a shared kiln room"
				width="560"
				height="360"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
			<h2>What makes a membership studio hard to run</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Everyone wants the same wheel</h3>
					<p>
						Weeknight evenings and Saturday mornings are packed, and a sign-up sheet on the wall
						means the same few members get the best slots while others give up.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>The kiln shelf is a mystery</h3>
					<p>
						Dozens of members share a few kilns. Nobody knows which load their bowl is in, firing
						fees get counted by hand, and finished work piles up waiting for pickup.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Classes and members collide</h3>
					<p>
						A Tuesday course takes over half the wheels, open-studio members turn up anyway, and
						you are answering the same scheduling emails every week.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Fair wheel time for every member</h2>
		<p>
			Members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and shared equipment in one-hour blocks from their
			phone. You set how many hours each membership tier gets, how far ahead they can book and
			whether evenings count double. A tablet by the door handles open-studio check-in, so you
			always know who is in the building.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel time works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Shared kilns without the shelf chaos</h2>
		<p>
			Members log each piece when they set it on the bisque shelf and pay the firing fee by cubic
			inch on the spot. Every kiln gets its own queue for bisque and glaze loads, and members get a
			text with a photo of the shelf when their work is ready to take home.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes that share the floor</h2>
		<p>
			Run six-week courses, drop-ins and class packs alongside open-studio hours. Waitlists fill
			cancelled seats on their own, and instructors see today's roster from the studio tablet.
			<a href="/features/classes">How classes and packs work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits?</h2>
		<p>
			Most community studios start on the Studio plan at $79 a month. It covers up to 3 kilns with
			unlimited members, wheel and table reservations, class packs, waitlists and memberships, and
			pickup texts. Smaller shared setups with one kiln and up to 150 members can use Starter, and
			studios with more kilns or more than one location move to Collective.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Give your members a studio they can book.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
